Snapshot replication : Create bcp files from source and put in destination server at certain time period. Useful for small applications. Any changes in source after snapshot ceation will not be copied to destination.

Snapshot agent reads the data from source and put in a snapshot folder using BCP

Transaction replication : It is unidirectional oneway , it replicate the transaction from source to destination after snaphot is created. whatever changes happen to transaction replication tables are copied to destination server.

sendig changes From source to destination.

Source is publisher and destination is subscriber. Publisher is the one who sents the data and subscriber the one receives the data.
Publisher will publish the data through publication. create subscription is subscriber.
Publication will have articles and it publish the data and subscriber subscribe to articles.
Articles are nothing but tables, procedure and views

When setup a transaction replication, it creates "Log reader agent" (LRA) process. LRA it will read the changes in publication and write into distribution database(like queue database).
It also create another process "distribution agent". It reads the data from distribution database and apply in target database.
"Log reader agent" (LRA) process will be in distributed database only.

We can put distribution database in below ways.
1. Distribution database in different server and publisher and subscriber(distribution agent here) in differnent servers -> Pull subscription
2. Distribution and publisher in same server and subscriber in differnent server(distribution agent here) -> Pull subscription
3. Distribution and publisher in same server(distribution agent here) and subscriber in differnent server -> Push subscription

If distribution agent is subscriber server then it is "PULL" and if distribution agent is in distributor server then it is "PUSH" subscription.

Log reader agent reads the data from ldf file using sp_replcommand from source the server and write into distribution database.
if you want to browse the commands whatever writing using sp_replbrowsecommand

In distribution we will have 2 tables to write data from sp_replcommand.
1. msrepl_commands
2. msrepl_transaction

distributor agent will reads data from these tables and write into subscriber target database.

Snapshot agent will do BCP files in snapshot folder and this folder will be in distribution database servers(either differnt server or same source server)
distributor agent will read BCP files and write into target server

